```
`parseInt()` coerces string inputs to base-10 integers. If a user passes `'3000; /usr/bin/genpoc'`, `parseInt()` evaluates it as `3000` and safely truncates everything after the first non-numeric character. This prevents shell metacharacters from ever reaching `exec()`, effectively neutralizing the injection vector.

