   The patch fixes #67 by introducing `prepareUserAgent(userAgent).substr(0, 500)`. This works because ReDoS requires a minimum input length to reach critical backtracking depth. Truncating to 500 characters ensures the regex engine never traverses far enough into the pattern to trigger exponential behavior, effectively neutralizing the attack surface regardless of how maliciously crafted the tail of the string might be.

